  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data above 298 K estimated except temperature and enthalpy of transition. \nPhase changes: 618 K, red - black transition point of HgS; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.000$ kcal/mol. \n629.81 K, boiling point of Hg; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 14.151$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-618 K: $Cp^{0} = 11.048 + 3.710 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.519 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=11.048\\times10^{-3}T+1.855\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.519\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-3.633$ \n618-900 K: $Cp^{0} = 11.761 + 2.856 \\times 10^{-3} T - 1.360 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=11.761\\times10^{-3}T+1.428\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+1.360\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-3.047$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-618 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -28.841 + 0.604 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} + 1.594 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 49.150 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -28.841 - 0.604 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} - 1.594 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 24.575 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 30.942 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n618-629.81 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -28.255 + 1.316 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} + 1.167 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 133.250 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -28.255 - 1.316 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} - 1.167 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 66.625 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 34.201 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{T}$ \n629.81-900 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -43.218 + 2.621 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} + 1.268 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 101.850 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -43.218 - 2.621 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{TlnT} - 1.268 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 50.925 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 66.474 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K based on Goldfinger (45), Mitchell (82), Treadwell (119), and Grade (46). Low-temperature heat capacities and entropy at 298 K from King (67). \n\nHigh-temperature data estimated except temperature and enthalpy of transition. ",
